## 3. Validation checklist

| # | Where | Check | Expected |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Bastion | `ls ~/evidence/lynis-*.dat` | Three `.dat` files: baseline, hardened, remediated |
| 2 | Bastion | Step E comparison loop | Index values recorded for all three |
| 3 | Bastion | Hardened index vs baseline | **Higher** (record the delta) |
| 4 | Bastion | Remediated index vs hardened | Higher or equal |
| 5 | Target | `sudo aide.wrapper --check` | No differences (right after init) |
| 6 | Target | `sudo sshd -T \| grep -i maxsessions` | `maxsessions 2` |
| 7 | Target | `sudo chage -l secadmin \| grep -E 'Maximum\|Minimum\|warning'` | 365 / 1 / 14 |
| 8 | Target | `cat /etc/issue.net` | Banner text present |
| 9 | Target | `bash -lc 'echo $TMOUT'` | `600` |
| 10 | Target | `dpkg -l libpam-pwquality needrestart debsums acct aide \| grep ^ii \| wc -l` | `5` or more |
| 11 | Both | Step E "what disappeared" count | Non-zero (hardening visibly removed findings) |
| 12 | Target | `ip route` after closing NAT | No default route |
| 13 | Target | Everything from Points 4 to 7 still working: `ssh target hostname` from the Bastion, `sudo ufw status`, `systemctl is-active fail2ban auditd`, `sudo auditctl -s \| grep enabled` | All healthy, `enabled 2` |
| 14 | Clone | `target-baseline` VM deleted | Yes, and no leftover VM running with IP `10.10.10.20` |

